$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ ST6/Babanin source terms with test-point output.
$
$ Purpose: this is the only registered case that reaches the SSWELL_*
$ routines. They sit behind IWCAP == 8, which only ST6/Babanin
$ whitecapping sets, and they are the only source-term kernels that need
$ TESTFL and IPTST to place their diagnostics. Every other test-point deck
$ in the suite runs GEN3 WESTH, so the swell-dissipation column of the
$ test output was unexercised until this case existed.
$
$ Synthetic 1D fetch-limited growth; not an observation or a design
$ condition.
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'ST6TEST' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 50000.0 0.0 250 0 &
      CIRCLE 36 0.04 1.0 34

INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 50 0 1000.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

WIND 15.0 0.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.5 5.0 0.0 20.0

$ ST6 wind input and whitecapping (IWCAP = 8), with Zieger swell
$ dissipation so SSWELL_ZIEGER is the active branch.
GEN3 ST6 4.7E-7 6.6E-6 4.0 4.0 UP HWANG VECTAU U10PROXY 28.0 AGROW
SSWELL ZIEGER
QUADRUPLET 3
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

POINTS 'GAUGES' 20000.0 0.0 40000.0 0.0 45000.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'st6_testpoints.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 GENW DISW DISSU DISB

$ The test point drives the source-term diagnostics. Column 4 of the S1D
$ file is the swell dissipation written by SSWELL_ZIEGER.
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 45000.0 0.0 S1D 'st6_testpoints_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
